>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `DEEPEN_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.DEEPEN_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by iteratively deepened classical search.

`DEEPEN_TAC thms` first safely saturates the state, then tries bounded
depth-first searches at bounds 4, 6, 8 and 10. Thus its default start is
4, increment is 2 and ceiling is 10. Matching safe steps and unifying
assumption, contradiction, and zero-premise safe steps consume no bound.
Positive-premise instantiating and duplicating unsafe steps consume one
unit on each branch. Search uses dynamic per-goal pruning and
stops at the first successful bound.

The lowercase `deepen_tac cs {start = n}` interface permits another start;
its increment and ceiling remain 2 and 10.

The theorem list locally processes `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` markers. Unmarked theorems become unsafe
introduction rules. Generic simplifier markers such as `Cong`, `Excl` and
`SF` are ignored by the classical reasoner.

The tactic succeeds only with a complete, replayed proof.

### Failure

Fails if none of the attempted bounds produces a complete proof. Malformed
extra rules can also fail while the temporary rule set is built.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem deepen_tac_example:
  (p ==> q) ==> (q ==> r) ==> p ==> r
Proof
  classicalLib.DEEPEN_TAC []
QED
```

